---
description: Scubiee GATE - when to use (how-to in MCP instructions)
alwaysApply: true
---

Policy only; tool how-to is in Scubiee MCP server instructions every turn.

- **GATE 0** - Not managed (no `scubiee init`). BAN Scubiee MCP locate tools (`map`, `focus`, `grep`, `glob`, `workspace`). USE native Grep/Glob/Read/codebase-search only. Run `scubiee init .` to enroll.
- **GATE 1:ce_*** (managed): When Scubiee tools are available, use them strictly by scenario (soft->pinpoint; how-X-works->plate; cards->map; path->host Read; exact->host Grep; name->host Glob). Native Grep/Glob/Read OK only if Scubiee MCP is down, blocked, paused, or errors - continue working; do not deadlock. Edit/Write/Shell stay native. How-to -> MCP server instructions.
- **GATE p** - Scubiee STOPPED (`scubiee stop`). BAN all Scubiee MCP tools (map, focus, pinpoint, plate, grep, glob, workspace, expand, search, read, files, recall, neighbors, graph, outline, status loops). USE native Read/Grep/Glob/codebase-search only. Run `scubiee resume` (NOT `init`).
